      "message": "[warning] Line 35: 🟡 When `fixedTransform` is cleared (`newValue \u003d\u003d nil`), `currentTransform` is left unchanged, but `syncGeometry()` still runs immediately. After switching from local-camera PiP to participant PiP, this can keep the old local-camera transform (mirror/rotation) applied until a new remote frame arrives, causing visibly wrong orientation. Reset `currentTransform` when clearing `fixedTransform` (or defer geometry sync until first frame of the new distributor) so the stale transform is never rendered.",
